Subject: [PENDING INTEGRATION] Preserve WAL quarantine provenance through detached cleanup (#510)
Base-Pager-Blob: fd6daead74625c9742983959a55aa90f6be19d99
Target: crates/fsqlite-pager/src/pager.rs

This is an unapplied production-and-regression candidate, not an installed fix.
The previous production commit d9837a6ec3a8116fb51586835fcb52f77a547294
repairs ordinary cleanup. Dropping a pending group-commit transaction instead
moves its reservations to DetachedPendingGroupCommitTxnCleanup, which currently
does not receive the durable-freelist origin set. NotCommitted cleanup sends
committed-free quarantine entries into EOF abandonment and loses that origin.

Carry the origin set until a terminal outcome is known. On NotCommitted return
committed-free quarantine entries through the existing restoration helper;
leave fresh EOF entries on the existing abandonment path. On Authorized retire
bookkeeping without recycling committed pages. Do not alter Pending outcome
classification, snapshot horizons, first-committer-wins validation, or defaults.

The regression drives the production transaction Drop/deferred-cleanup boundary
with the existing mock-WAL fixture and a pre-admission receipt. It checks no
early return, exact-once restoration, distinct EOF handling, no publication of
discarded writes, and subsequent allocation/write on the same pager. This is
NOT a native I/O-cancellation, power-loss, or SQL/index interoperability test.

Status: source-reviewed against the blob above; unified-diff syntax checked.
No complete-checkout apply check, Rust compilation, rustfmt, Clippy, or runtime
pass is claimed. Cargo and RCH are unavailable in the preparation environment.
